<overview>
<p>Infantry equipped with microlite aircraft that are little more than a hang glider with a pusher prop engine can roam even the most restrictive terrain at will - providing the weather cooperates. The ultra-short take off and landing capability allows them to stage from areas that prohibit conventional aircraft, and their slower, highly maneuverable nature mean they can safely operate much closer to the ground, slipping around hills and through valleys unobserved. Weight limits restrict the use of heavy support weapons making them suited to observation and similar roles rather than direct combat.</p><p>Equipped with laser rifles that offer superior range and armor penetration compared to ballistic weapons, these platoons field one of the most effective personal arms available to conventional infantry, though the weapons are significantly more expensive and require soldiers to carry additional power packs.</p>
</overview>

<notes>
Intro date based on prototype date of generic Laser Rifle weapon
</notes>

